{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And you shall keep the Sabbath.</b> After he mentioned את שבתותי תשמרו — 'you shall keep My Sabbaths' — he returned to say ושמרתם את השבת, in order to hint at keeping after the Sabbath and keeping before the Sabbath: keeping before the Sabbath, while it is still day; and keeping after the Sabbath, that one adds from the profane onto the holy. And so our Rabbis of blessed memory expounded: ״לא ימיש עמוד הענן יומם ועמוד האש לילה״ — this teaches that the pillar of cloud completes for the pillar of fire, and likewise the pillar of fire completes for the pillar of cloud: before this one sets, that one rises. And so they expounded: ״מערב עד ערב תשבתו שבתכם״ — 'your Sabbath' I have only the Day of Atonement, and this is 'from evening to evening'; festivals, whence do I know? Scripture says ״תשבתו״; I have only a festival, the Sabbath of Creation, whence? Scripture says ״שבתכם״ — for any rest that you rest, you add to it, whether before it or after it." "<b>whoever profanes it shall surely be put to death, for whoever does work in it shall be cut off.</b> Scripture explained: ״מחלליה מות יומת״ — by stoning, if there are witnesses and warning; and if there are no witnesses, such as one who acted in secret — ״ונכרתה הנפש ההיא״, that soul shall be cut off."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:06:03.267736378Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}